From: Neutron lab (ai58)
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp, winewayland.drv: copy a D3D12 swap chain when children sit over it; never put a chain the bridge cannot read below the window surface

What he saw (Neutron#58, reporter's words): "Illustrator Type Tool causes editing area to return to welcome screen."
Illustrator 2027 (31.0.0.84), GPU Performance on, New Document, Type tool, click the artboard and type: the document
area shows Illustrator's Home screen (white with "Show The Home Screen When No Documents Are Open" off); clicking
brings the canvas back for a moment. CPU view (Ctrl+E) does not do it.

Mechanism (SOLID, lab):
- The canvas is a DroverLord "OS_ViewContainer" child (WS_CLIPCHILDREN) presenting a vkd3d-proton D3D12 swap chain
  for its own window; DXVK's dxgi registers it with the dcomp bridge (dcomp-hook PresentBase is_d3d12=1), so the
  window gets the __wine_dcomp_blit mark ("the bridge can copy its frames").
- The Type tool shows the on-canvas type bar; its font-size field is a real Edit child (OS_EditTextContainer > Edit,
  81x31) over the canvas. children-over-chain then puts the chain's client surface BELOW the window surface and
  leaves the canvas to the bridge's copy through the window's DC.
- The bridge reads a chain as an ID3D11Texture2D. A D3D12 chain's buffers are ID3D12Resource: GetBuffer answers
  E_NOINTERFACE ("diag: GetBuffer failed hr 0x80004002") and nothing is copied, so the window surface's old pixels
  show: the Home page drawn into that area earlier (CEF frames blitted into the top-level), or the white fill.
  When the field hides (click elsewhere), the client surface goes back above and the canvas returns.
Windows: DWM composes every swap chain itself and child windows above it (the field shows over the canvas).

Fix:
1. dcomp: read back a D3D12 chain (8-bit BGRA/RGBA, single-sampled): the buffer it presented last (the one before
   its current back buffer), copied with CopyTextureRegion into a readback buffer on a direct queue the bridge owns
   on the chain's device, waited on a fence (250 ms cap); the same-process GDI path then draws it, clipped by the
   children. The bridge cannot reach the app's queue (vkd3d-proton's IDXGISwapChain::GetDevice answers with the
   device), so the copy has no GPU ordering against the app's rendering; it runs one blit tick (16 ms) after the
   Present that marked it. The presented buffer is in PRESENT (= COMMON), which promotes to COPY_SOURCE implicitly.
2. dcomp: mark a window __wine_dcomp_blit only while its chain can be read the way the bridge reads it (D3D11
   texture, or a D3D12 chain that (1) handles); otherwise take the mark back. An unreadable chain stays on its own
   client surface, as patch 150 leaves every direct chain.
3. winewayland: children-over-chain keys on the LIVE mark, not the sticky latch, so a taken-back mark is honored.

Not covered: D3D12 chains in 10-bit/FP16 formats (unmarked: their children stay hidden under the chain, the
pre-children-copy behavior); the D3D12 copy is not GPU-ordered with the app's queue (a frame the app has not
finished rendering 16 ms after its Present is read as it stands; not seen in the lab); the copy costs a readback per
present while children cover the chain (2410x1880 here); GNOME (the reporter's desktop) not run, KDE nested only;
hybrid Intel+NVIDIA not run (lab GPU = one NVIDIA).

Lab (desk: one 3840x2160 output at scale 2.0 = 192 dpi like the reporter; prefix copy of a signed-in Ai 2026 + 2027
lab prefix provisioned per runtime with CLI beta.43; steps: Ctrl+N, Create, T, click artboard, type ffff, Escape,
click; shots after each step):
  Illustrator 2027 31.0.0.84 (signed-in lab copy), GPU Performance on:
    217 plain r1 r2                                   Home screen in the document area 2/2 (2 % white), canvas back after
                                                      Escape + click; "GetBuffer failed hr 0x80004002"
    217, CPU view (Ctrl+E) c1                         canvas fine 1/1 (the reporter's workaround), 0 children-copy switches
    225 plain b1 b2                                   Home screen 2/2 (225 does not fix it)
    225aj (225 + this patch) j2 j3                    canvas, text and the type bar's "12 pt" field drawn 2/2, same as the
                                                      CPU view; "neutron-d3d12-copy: 2410x1880 format 87 -> read back"
    225aj NEUTRON_DCOMP_D3D12_COPY=0 k1 k3            canvas and text fine, the "12 pt" field EMPTY 2/2 (the Edit child
                                                      under the chain; 0 below switches)
    225aj D3D12_COPY=0 + NEUTRON_DCOMP_MARK_READABLE=0 k2 k4   Home screen 2/2 (== 225)
  Illustrator 2026 30.8.2 (same prefix, 2027 folder moved aside):
    217 a9 a10 a11                                    artboard gone, flat gray document area with the "12 pt / 1 pt"
                                                      chip on it 3/3, back after Escape + click
    225aj a7 a8                                       artboard and type bar with "12 pt" 2/2; D3D12 copy 3226x1880
  Every run quit clean (td CLEAN). Lab runtimes: 11.10-225ai (parts 2+3 only), 11.10-225aj (whole patch).
Not run: regression on other apps (no other lab app is known to present a D3D12 chain with children over it; the
change is limited to windows with a D3D12 chain: 8-bit ones now copied while children cover them, others no longer
marked); GNOME; NVIDIA+Intel hybrid.
Kill switches: NEUTRON_DCOMP_D3D12_COPY=0 (no D3D12 readback: the chain stays on its own client surface, children
hidden under it), NEUTRON_DCOMP_MARK_READABLE=0 (mark every same-process chain, as 225; with both off == 225).

Regression, lab rel58 (11-23; desk = the owner's layout: 3840x2160 at 175 % (168 dpi) + 1920x1080 at 100 %; one prefix copy per
pair provisioned on 225 with CLI 3f9a1af, fresh reflink per run; matched screenshots pixel-diffed, every non-zero diff viewed),
225 (A) vs 225aj (B):
  Illustrator 2027 + 2026, GPU and CPU view, Type tool, Character panel, font menu: only the typing shots differ (225: Home screen /
    gray area; 225aj: artboard, text and type bar), every other step 0 px.
  Photoshop (text layer, contextual task bar, brush, Camera Raw, Open/Save As, prefs), After Effects (OCIO ACES 1.2, import, comp,
    layer selected, Effects & Presets, Render Queue), Lightroom Classic (Develop on a real file, Masking brush, filmstrip),
    Premiere (timeline, Effect Controls, program monitor playing), Animate (stage): every difference also occurs between two runs of
    the same runtime (promo video frame, Tip of the Day, sample carousel, thumbnails, LrC panel gutter, playback position) or is a
    slower app start; n=2 pairs where anything differed. Photoshop, Lightroom Classic and Animate present D3D12 chains too; no
    children-over-chain switch fired for them in either arm.
  Cost (Illustrator 2027, 40-character bursts with the type bar over the canvas): +0.75 s CPU per 4.7 s burst and +1 s per 10 s idle
    vs 225 (which copies nothing); at or below the CPU view (the reporter's workaround); no visible typing lag; equal without the type bar.
Also applies to 11.10-217.1's dlls/dcomp/device.c and dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c with offsets only (patch -F0); the
patched text equals 225's patched text up to the files' existing 217/225 differences (11.10-217.2 pre-release).
---
--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
@@ -32,6 +32,8 @@
 #include "objbase.h"
 #include "dxgi.h"
 #include "d3d11.h"
+#include "dxgi1_4.h"
+#include "d3d12.h"
 #include "dcomp.h"
 #include "wine/list.h"
 #include "wine/debug.h"
@@ -603,6 +605,273 @@
 };
 struct INeutronBoundedAcquire { const struct INeutronBoundedAcquireVtbl *lpVtbl; };
 
+/* NEUTRON 2026-11-23 (Neutron#58): read back a D3D12 swap chain, so children-over-chain can copy it like a D3D11
+ * one. Illustrator 2027's (and 2026's DirectXRenderer) canvas is a vkd3d-proton D3D12 chain made for its own
+ * window; the Type tool puts an Edit child (the font-size field of the on-canvas type bar) over it. Windows
+ * composes that child above the chain. Here the child is GDI content of the top-level's window surface, so the
+ * chain goes below that surface and must reach it through the window's DC -- which needs its pixels.
+ * The copy reads the buffer the chain presented last (the one before its current back buffer) on a direct queue
+ * of the chain's device that the bridge owns: the app's own queue is not reachable (vkd3d-proton's
+ * IDXGISwapChain::GetDevice answers with the device). The buffer is in the PRESENT (= COMMON) state, which
+ * promotes to COPY_SOURCE implicitly and decays back at the end of the submission. The bridge reads it one blit
+ * tick (16 ms) after its Present, without a GPU wait on the app's queue: a frame the app has not finished
+ * rendering by then is read as it stands. 8-bit BGRA/RGBA chains only.
+ * Kill switch NEUTRON_DCOMP_D3D12_COPY=0 (no D3D12 readback: such a chain is not copyable and stays on its own
+ * client surface). */
+static int neutron_d3d12_copy(void)
+{
+    static int gate = -1;
+
+    if (gate < 0)
+    {
+        char b[8];
+        gate = (GetEnvironmentVariableA("NEUTRON_DCOMP_D3D12_COPY", b, sizeof(b)) && b[0] == '0') ? 0 : 1;
+        ERR("neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_DCOMP_D3D12_COPY = %d\n", gate);
+    }
+    return gate;
+}
+
+static BOOL neutron_d3d12_format_ok(DXGI_FORMAT format, BOOL *swap_rb)
+{
+    switch (format)
+    {
+    case DXGI_FORMAT_B8G8R8A8_UNORM: case DXGI_FORMAT_B8G8R8A8_UNORM_SRGB:
+    case DXGI_FORMAT_B8G8R8X8_UNORM: case DXGI_FORMAT_B8G8R8X8_UNORM_SRGB:
+        *swap_rb = FALSE;
+        return TRUE;
+    case DXGI_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM: case DXGI_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM_SRGB:
+        *swap_rb = TRUE;
+        return TRUE;
+    default:
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+}
+
+/* The buffer a D3D12 (flip-model) chain presented last, with its description. */
+static ID3D12Resource *neutron_d3d12_presented(IDXGISwapChain *swapchain, D3D12_RESOURCE_DESC *rd)
+{
+    DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_DESC scd;
+    IDXGISwapChain3 *sc3 = NULL;
+    ID3D12Resource *res = NULL;
+    UINT index = 0;
+
+    if (FAILED(IDXGISwapChain_GetDesc(swapchain, &scd))) return NULL;
+    if (scd.BufferCount > 1 && SUCCEEDED(IDXGISwapChain_QueryInterface(swapchain, &IID_IDXGISwapChain3, (void **)&sc3)))
+    {
+        index = (IDXGISwapChain3_GetCurrentBackBufferIndex(sc3) + scd.BufferCount - 1) % scd.BufferCount;
+        IDXGISwapChain3_Release(sc3);
+    }
+    if (FAILED(IDXGISwapChain_GetBuffer(swapchain, index, &IID_ID3D12Resource, (void **)&res)) || !res) return NULL;
+    res->lpVtbl->GetDesc(res, rd);
+    return res;
+}
+
+static struct
+{
+    CRITICAL_SECTION cs;
+    ID3D12Device *device;
+    ID3D12CommandQueue *queue;
+    ID3D12CommandAllocator *allocator;
+    ID3D12GraphicsCommandList *list;
+    ID3D12Resource *buffer;
+    UINT64 buffer_size;
+    ID3D12Fence *fence;
+    UINT64 value;
+    HANDLE event;
+    BOOL busy; /* a copy that did not finish in time still owns the allocator */
+} d3d12_rb;
+static INIT_ONCE d3d12_rb_once = INIT_ONCE_STATIC_INIT;
+
+static BOOL CALLBACK d3d12_rb_init(INIT_ONCE *once, void *param, void **context)
+{
+    InitializeCriticalSection(&d3d12_rb.cs);
+    d3d12_rb.event = CreateEventW(NULL, FALSE, FALSE, NULL);
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
+static void d3d12_rb_release(void)
+{
+    if (d3d12_rb.list) ID3D12GraphicsCommandList_Release(d3d12_rb.list);
+    if (d3d12_rb.allocator) ID3D12CommandAllocator_Release(d3d12_rb.allocator);
+    if (d3d12_rb.buffer) ID3D12Resource_Release(d3d12_rb.buffer);
+    if (d3d12_rb.fence) ID3D12Fence_Release(d3d12_rb.fence);
+    if (d3d12_rb.queue) ID3D12CommandQueue_Release(d3d12_rb.queue);
+    if (d3d12_rb.device) ID3D12Device_Release(d3d12_rb.device);
+    d3d12_rb.queue = NULL; d3d12_rb.list = NULL; d3d12_rb.allocator = NULL; d3d12_rb.buffer = NULL; d3d12_rb.fence = NULL;
+    d3d12_rb.device = NULL; d3d12_rb.buffer_size = 0; d3d12_rb.value = 0; d3d12_rb.busy = FALSE;
+}
+
+/* Returns the presented frame as packed BGRA rows (malloc'd, caller frees) and its size, or NULL. */
+static void *neutron_d3d12_readback(IDXGISwapChain *swapchain, UINT *width, UINT *height)
+{
+    static unsigned int nlog;
+    D3D12_HEAP_PROPERTIES heap = {D3D12_HEAP_TYPE_READBACK};
+    D3D12_PLACED_SUBRESOURCE_FOOTPRINT fp;
+    D3D12_TEXTURE_COPY_LOCATION dst, src;
+    D3D12_COMMAND_QUEUE_DESC qd = {D3D12_COMMAND_LIST_TYPE_DIRECT};
+    D3D12_RESOURCE_DESC rd, bd;
+    D3D12_RANGE range;
+    ID3D12Device *device = NULL;
+    ID3D12Resource *res;
+    UINT64 row_size, total;
+    BYTE *mapped = NULL, *packed = NULL;
+    UINT rows, x, y;
+    BOOL swap_rb;
+    HRESULT hr = E_FAIL;
+
+    if (!(res = neutron_d3d12_presented(swapchain, &rd))) return NULL;
+    if (rd.Dimension != D3D12_RESOURCE_DIMENSION_TEXTURE2D || rd.SampleDesc.Count != 1
+            || !neutron_d3d12_format_ok(rd.Format, &swap_rb) || !rd.Width || !rd.Height)
+        goto out;
+    if (FAILED(hr = ID3D12Resource_GetDevice(res, &IID_ID3D12Device, (void **)&device))) goto out;
+    ID3D12Device_GetCopyableFootprints(device, &rd, 0, 1, 0, &fp, &rows, &row_size, &total);
+
+    InitOnceExecuteOnce(&d3d12_rb_once, d3d12_rb_init, NULL, NULL);
+    EnterCriticalSection(&d3d12_rb.cs);
+    if (d3d12_rb.busy)
+    {
+        if (ID3D12Fence_GetCompletedValue(d3d12_rb.fence) < d3d12_rb.value) { hr = E_PENDING; goto unlock; }
+        d3d12_rb.busy = FALSE;
+    }
+    if (d3d12_rb.device != device)
+    {
+        d3d12_rb_release();
+        if (FAILED(hr = ID3D12Device_CreateCommandQueue(device, &qd, &IID_ID3D12CommandQueue, (void **)&d3d12_rb.queue))
+                || FAILED(hr = ID3D12Device_CreateCommandAllocator(device, qd.Type, &IID_ID3D12CommandAllocator,
+                (void **)&d3d12_rb.allocator))
+                || FAILED(hr = ID3D12Device_CreateCommandList(device, 0, qd.Type, d3d12_rb.allocator, NULL,
+                &IID_ID3D12GraphicsCommandList, (void **)&d3d12_rb.list))
+                || FAILED(hr = ID3D12GraphicsCommandList_Close(d3d12_rb.list))
+                || FAILED(hr = ID3D12Device_CreateFence(device, 0, D3D12_FENCE_FLAG_NONE, &IID_ID3D12Fence,
+                (void **)&d3d12_rb.fence)))
+        {
+            d3d12_rb_release();
+            goto unlock;
+        }
+        ID3D12Device_AddRef(device);
+        d3d12_rb.device = device;
+    }
+    if (d3d12_rb.buffer_size < total)
+    {
+        if (d3d12_rb.buffer) ID3D12Resource_Release(d3d12_rb.buffer);
+        d3d12_rb.buffer = NULL; d3d12_rb.buffer_size = 0;
+        memset(&bd, 0, sizeof(bd));
+        bd.Dimension = D3D12_RESOURCE_DIMENSION_BUFFER;
+        bd.Width = total;
+        bd.Height = 1;
+        bd.DepthOrArraySize = 1;
+        bd.MipLevels = 1;
+        bd.SampleDesc.Count = 1;
+        bd.Layout = D3D12_TEXTURE_LAYOUT_ROW_MAJOR;
+        if (FAILED(hr = ID3D12Device_CreateCommittedResource(device, &heap, D3D12_HEAP_FLAG_NONE, &bd,
+                D3D12_RESOURCE_STATE_COPY_DEST, NULL, &IID_ID3D12Resource, (void **)&d3d12_rb.buffer)))
+            goto unlock;
+        d3d12_rb.buffer_size = total;
+    }
+    if (FAILED(hr = ID3D12CommandAllocator_Reset(d3d12_rb.allocator))
+            || FAILED(hr = ID3D12GraphicsCommandList_Reset(d3d12_rb.list, d3d12_rb.allocator, NULL)))
+        goto unlock;
+    dst.pResource = d3d12_rb.buffer;
+    dst.Type = D3D12_TEXTURE_COPY_TYPE_PLACED_FOOTPRINT;
+    dst.PlacedFootprint = fp;
+    src.pResource = res;
+    src.Type = D3D12_TEXTURE_COPY_TYPE_SUBRESOURCE_INDEX;
+    src.SubresourceIndex = 0;
+    ID3D12GraphicsCommandList_CopyTextureRegion(d3d12_rb.list, &dst, 0, 0, 0, &src, NULL);
+    if (FAILED(hr = ID3D12GraphicsCommandList_Close(d3d12_rb.list))) goto unlock;
+    ID3D12CommandQueue_ExecuteCommandLists(d3d12_rb.queue, 1, (ID3D12CommandList **)&d3d12_rb.list);
+    if (FAILED(hr = ID3D12CommandQueue_Signal(d3d12_rb.queue, d3d12_rb.fence, ++d3d12_rb.value))) goto unlock;
+    if (ID3D12Fence_GetCompletedValue(d3d12_rb.fence) < d3d12_rb.value)
+    {
+        ID3D12Fence_SetEventOnCompletion(d3d12_rb.fence, d3d12_rb.value, d3d12_rb.event);
+        if (WaitForSingleObject(d3d12_rb.event, 250) != WAIT_OBJECT_0)
+        {
+            d3d12_rb.busy = TRUE; /* dropped; the next readback waits for it first */
+            hr = E_PENDING;
+            goto unlock;
+        }
+    }
+    range.Begin = 0;
+    range.End = total;
+    if (FAILED(hr = ID3D12Resource_Map(d3d12_rb.buffer, 0, &range, (void **)&mapped))) goto unlock;
+    if ((packed = malloc((SIZE_T)rd.Width * 4 * rd.Height)))
+    {
+        for (y = 0; y < rd.Height; y++)
+        {
+            const BYTE *row = mapped + fp.Offset + (SIZE_T)y * fp.Footprint.RowPitch;
+            DWORD *out = (DWORD *)(packed + (SIZE_T)y * rd.Width * 4);
+
+            memcpy(out, row, (SIZE_T)rd.Width * 4);
+            if (swap_rb)
+                for (x = 0; x < rd.Width; x++)
+                    out[x] = (out[x] & 0xff00ff00) | ((out[x] & 0xff) << 16) | ((out[x] >> 16) & 0xff);
+        }
+        *width = rd.Width;
+        *height = rd.Height;
+    }
+    range.End = 0;
+    ID3D12Resource_Unmap(d3d12_rb.buffer, 0, &range);
+unlock:
+    LeaveCriticalSection(&d3d12_rb.cs);
+out:
+    if (nlog < 8 && (!packed || !nlog))
+    {
+        nlog++;
+        ERR("neutron-d3d12-copy: swapchain=%p %ux%u format %u -> %s (hr %#lx)\n", swapchain, (UINT)rd.Width,
+            rd.Height, rd.Format, packed ? "read back" : "not read", hr);
+    }
+    if (device) ID3D12Device_Release(device);
+    ID3D12Resource_Release(res);
+    return packed;
+}
+
+/* NEUTRON 2026-11-23 (Neutron#58, Illustrator 2027 Type tool): the bridge copies a chain by asking it for an
+ * ID3D11Texture2D (blit_swapchain_to_hwnd). A D3D12 chain -- vkd3d-proton's, which DXVK's dxgi registers here
+ * (dcomp-hook PresentBase is_d3d12=1) -- has ID3D12Resource buffers: GetBuffer answers E_NOINTERFACE and the
+ * bridge copies nothing. The __wine_dcomp_blit mark tells winewayland that the bridge CAN copy a window's chain;
+ * children-over-chain puts a marked chain's client surface below the window surface once a child sits over it,
+ * which for a D3D12 chain bared whatever the window surface held (Illustrator's Home page drawn there earlier,
+ * or white). Mark a window only while its chain can be read the way the bridge reads it; an unreadable chain
+ * stays on its own client surface, as patch 150 leaves every direct chain. Windows: DWM composes every chain,
+ * nothing copies it. Kill switch NEUTRON_DCOMP_MARK_READABLE=0 (mark every same-process chain, as before). */
+static BOOL neutron_chain_readable(IDXGISwapChain *swapchain, HWND hwnd)
+{
+    static int gate = -1;
+    ID3D11Texture2D *tex = NULL;
+    HRESULT hr;
+
+    if (gate < 0)
+    {
+        char b[8];
+        gate = (GetEnvironmentVariableA("NEUTRON_DCOMP_MARK_READABLE", b, sizeof(b)) && b[0] == '0') ? 0 : 1;
+        ERR("neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_DCOMP_MARK_READABLE = %d\n", gate);
+    }
+    if (!gate) return TRUE;
+    hr = IDXGISwapChain_GetBuffer(swapchain, 0, &IID_ID3D11Texture2D, (void **)&tex);
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && tex)
+    {
+        ID3D11Texture2D_Release(tex);
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+    if (hr == E_NOINTERFACE && neutron_d3d12_copy())
+    {
+        D3D12_RESOURCE_DESC rd;
+        ID3D12Resource *res = neutron_d3d12_presented(swapchain, &rd);
+        BOOL swap_rb, ok = res && rd.Dimension == D3D12_RESOURCE_DIMENSION_TEXTURE2D && rd.SampleDesc.Count == 1
+                && neutron_d3d12_format_ok(rd.Format, &swap_rb);
+
+        if (res) ID3D12Resource_Release(res);
+        if (ok) return TRUE;
+    }
+    {
+        static unsigned int nlog;
+        if (nlog++ < 16)
+            ERR("neutron-unreadable: hwnd=%p swapchain=%p GetBuffer(ID3D11Texture2D) hr %#lx -> not marked, the bridge "
+                "cannot copy it (its own client surface shows it)\n", hwnd, swapchain, hr);
+    }
+    return FALSE;
+}
+
 /* Stamp a swapchain as bridge-managed. Returns 1 if DXVK acknowledged. */
 static int neutron_stamp_bounded_acquire(IDXGISwapChain *swapchain)
 {
@@ -865,7 +1134,11 @@
             }
             if (FAILED(hr))
             {
-                if (diag) ERR("diag: GetBuffer failed hr %#lx\n", hr);
+                /* Neutron#58: a D3D12 chain has ID3D12Resource buffers (see neutron_d3d12_readback) */
+                if (hr == E_NOINTERFACE && !p->cross_proc && neutron_d3d12_copy()
+                        && (packed = neutron_d3d12_readback(swapchain, &desc.Width, &desc.Height)))
+                    have_pixels = TRUE;
+                else if (diag) ERR("diag: GetBuffer failed hr %#lx\n", hr);
             }
             else
             {
@@ -1724,7 +1997,10 @@
      * the whole UI). The bridge already delivers content via GetDC+StretchDIBits, so
      * the client subsurface is redundant AND harmful; the mark lets winewayland drop
      * it (env NEUTRON_DCOMP_SUPPRESS_CLIENT=1) so the GDI content shows. */
-    if (!target_cross_proc && hwnd && !neutron_dcomp_native()) /* round-35: native mode never marks/suppresses same-proc windows */
+    if (!target_cross_proc && hwnd && !neutron_dcomp_native() /* round-35: native mode never marks/suppresses same-proc windows */
+            && !neutron_chain_readable(swapchain, hwnd))
+        RemovePropW(hwnd, L"__wine_dcomp_blit"); /* Neutron#58: an earlier, readable chain's mark */
+    else if (!target_cross_proc && hwnd && !neutron_dcomp_native())
     {
         SetPropW(hwnd, L"__wine_dcomp_blit", (HANDLE)(ULONG_PTR)1);
         /* NEUTRON diag: log every window we MARK for suppression, once per hwnd, so a
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -5231,7 +5231,9 @@
              * chain to this client surface (patch 150). Kill switch NEUTRON_DCOMP_CHILDREN_COPY=0. */
             static const WCHAR dcomp_below_prop[] =
                 {'_','_','w','i','n','e','_','d','c','o','m','p','_','b','e','l','o','w',0};
-            BOOL below = (marked || sticky) && visible && neutron_children_over_chain(hwnd);
+            /* Neutron#58: the LIVE mark, not the sticky latch -- dcomp takes the mark back when the window's chain
